This register lists known compromises the team accepted on purpose.

| ID | Debt | Why accepted | Consequence if left | Next action / milestone | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| TD-001 | Failed-login lockout (`LoginAttemptService`) is kept in memory. | Simple, and enough for one app instance in M3. | The count resets when the app restarts, and is not shared if a second instance runs. | M4: store attempts in the database, or use a rate-limit filter. | Donya |
| TD-002 | The Staff and Management views also filter the list they get back from the server. | The server-side filter endpoint (FR006/FR013) was not merged when the views were built. | All rows in the role's scope are downloaded. Slow with large data. | Remove the client filter once the server filter has its API test. | Donya / Adolf |
| TD-003 | `RequestDetail.jsx` and `MyRequests.jsx` are still placeholders, so request IDs in the lists are not clickable. | Outside the access-control slice. | Staff and Management cannot open a request from the list yet (FR007). | Build the detail and requester views. | [Team to assign] |
| TD-004 | CSRF protection is switched off for the JSON API. The session cookie is set to SameSite=Strict and HttpOnly instead. | Simpler for a single-page app on the same site. SameSite=Strict stops other sites sending the cookie. | Older browsers that ignore SameSite would be open to cross-site requests. | M4: turn on Spring CSRF tokens if the app is served from a different site. | Donya |
| TD-005 | Checkstyle, npm audit and dependency review warn but do not block merges. | A2 Task 4: warn first, block once a clean baseline exists. | New warnings can be merged unnoticed. | Make them blocking after the first clean run. | Donya |
| TD-006 | Demo/H2 has no DB-level append-only protection for NFR004; only app-layer writes enforce it there. Postgres profile applies `migration-postgres` V2 (nullable `from_status` + UPDATE/DELETE triggers). | H2 cannot run PostgreSQL triggers; demo stays friction-free. | NFR004 DB evidence is valid only against the postgres profile / real PostgreSQL. | Decide whether CI/evidence runs against real PostgreSQL (open test-DB question). | Adolf / Donya |
